  "description": "A doorstop spring flicked with a toe: the cartoon boing. 0 ms: the coil is bent and let go with a metallic twang; it whips back and forth so the pitch wobbles widely about seven times a second, the wobble dying over 600 ms while the whole note sags a little; the coil's overtones run away sharp of the pitch and chirp, the way spring reverbs do; a short plastic thunk from the skirting board it is screwed to.",
